      "06:58 — **No curry leaf. What about turmeric & pepper?**  \nPartner, clear answer 👇\n\n---\n\n## 🌕 Turmeric Powder (Manjal)\n\n### ✅ Can add — but VERY little\n- Just a **small pinch (not ½ tsp!)**\n- Too much → bitter + strange colour in wheat dosa\n\n### Why add?\n- Mild earth flavour\n- Slight golden colour\n- Anti-inflammatory benefit (minor effect at this quantity)\n\n👉 Mix directly into batter.\n\n---\n\n## 🌶️ Pepper Powder (Milagu)\n\n### ✅ Good addition — especially with ginger\n- Add **¼ tsp freshly crushed**\n- Not too much — wheat + excess pepper = harsh taste\n\n### Why good?\n- Improves digestion  \n- Adds warm heat (not chilli heat)  \n- Balances onion sweetness  \n\n👉 Add directly into batter.\n\n---\n\n## 🔬 Best Balanced Combo (No Curry Leaf Version)\n\nFor 1 cup wheat flour:\n\n- Salt – ½ tsp  \n- Jeera – ½ tsp  \n- Ginger – ½ tsp  \n- Green chilli – 1  \n- Onion – 2 tbsp  \n- Turmeric – tiny pinch  \n- Pepper – ¼ tsp  \n- Water – 1.75 cups (thin batter)  \n\nCook with ghee.\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Important Logic\n\n| If you want | Add | Avoid |\n|-------------|------|--------|\n| Soft | Less pepper | High heat |\n| Crispy | Slightly more water | Thick batter |\n| Mild | No pepper | — |\n| Spicy | Pepper + chilli | Too much turmeric |\n\n---\n\nThis becomes almost like **pepper wheat dosa** — very good for cold morning.\n\nIf you tell me — crispy thin or soft thick? I’ll fine-tune flame + water exactly."
     ]
