      "13/02/2026 06:27 — **Kodumai (Wheat) Dosai** 🌾  \nPartner, simple, soft, quick version — no fermentation required.\n\n---\n\n## 🌾 1) Instant Wheat Dosai (Soft Morning Version)\n\nimage_group{\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"wheat dosa\",\"godhuma dosa south indian\",\"instant wheat dosa thin crispy\",\"godhuma dosa with chutney\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\n\n### 🧂 Ingredients (1–2 persons)\n- Whole wheat flour – 1 cup (120 g)\n- Water – 1.5 to 2 cups (thin batter)\n- Salt – ½ tsp\n- Jeera – ½ tsp\n- Green chilli – 1 (finely chopped)\n- Curry leaves – few (optional)\n- Onion – 2 tbsp finely chopped (optional)\n- Ghee – for cooking\n\n⏱️ Prep Time: 5 mins  \n⏱️ Cooking Time: 10 mins  \n\n---\n\n### 🔥 Method (Important Texture Logic)\n\n1. **Mix batter**\n   - Add water gradually.\n   - Batter must be **thin like rava dosa batter** — slightly watery, not thick.\n   - Rest 5 minutes.\n\n2. **Heat tawa properly**\n   - Medium-high.\n   - Lightly smear ghee.\n\n3. **Pour like rava dosa**\n   - Do NOT spread thick.\n   - Pour from outside → inside in circular motion.\n   - Small holes are normal.\n\n4. **Drizzle ghee**\n   - Cook till golden edges.\n   - Flip only if needed (thin version usually one-side enough).\n\n---\n\n### 🧠 Texture Science\n- Thin batter → lace texture  \n- Thick batter → soft chapati-like dosa  \n- High heat first → crisp edges  \n- Medium finish → inside cooks without raw wheat smell  \n\n---\n\n## 🌾 2) Soft Dinner Version (Slightly Thick)\n\nIf you want soft, chapati-style dosa:\n\n- Reduce water (1.25 cup)\n- Spread gently like normal dosa\n- Cook both sides\n- Add little extra ghee\n\nGood for:\n- With curd\n- With mild chutney\n- For night digestion\n\n---\n\n## 🌿 Optional Upgrade (Hotel Touch)\nAdd:\n- 1 tbsp rice flour → crispy\n- 1 tbsp curd → softness\n- Pinch sugar → colour\n\n---\n\n## 🕰️ Morning vs Night Rule (Wheat Version)\n\n| Time | Texture | Why |\n|------|---------|------|\n| Morning | Thin crispy | Light on stomach |\n| Lunch | Medium | Filling |\n| Night | Soft | Easy digestion |\n\n---\n\nIf you tell me what ingredients you currently have (jeera? onion? curd? chilli powder?) I’ll tune exact ratio like we did for rasam."
     ]
    },
